.SH "NAME"
abrt-action-save-package-data \- Query package database and save package and component name\&.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
\fIabrt\-action\-save\-package\-data\fR [\-v] [\-c CONFFILE] \-d DIR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
The tool reads problem directory DIR\&. It analyzes contents of \fIanalyzer\fR, \fIexecutable\fR, \fIcmdline\fR and \fIremote\fR elements, checks database of installed packages, and creates new elements \fIpackage\fR and \fIcomponent\fR\&.
.sp
This data is usually necessary if the problem will be reported to a bug tracking database\&.
.SS "Integration with ABRT events"
.sp
This tool can be used as an ABRT reporter\&. Example fragment for \fI/etc/libreport/report_event\&.conf\fR:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
# Determine in which package/component the crash happened (if not yet done):
EVENT=post\-create component=
        abrt\-action\-save\-package\-data
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\-v, \-\-verbose
.RS 4
Be verbose
.RE
.PP
\-c CONFFILE
.RS 4
Path to configuration file\&.
.RE
.PP
\-r CHROOT
.RS 4
Force RPM to use CHROOT for root directory
.RE
.PP
\-d DIR
.RS 4
Path to problem directory\&.
.RE
